        "gui": {
          // The closed gate and its posts lie along X in a two pixel slab, the same layout as a pane. Yaw 135 is the turn that showed a pane's face the way the vanilla icon does; the usual 225 puts the gate's face on the other side of the icon.
          "rotation": [
            30,
            135,
            0
          ],
          // No offset. With fit_to_frame off the gate keeps its block coordinates and stands where the vanilla icon does. Since Minecraft 1.26.50 the translation moves the icon by slot pixels, so an offset here slides the whole gate rather than settling it.
